The s7 row in the engine table: $(s7 chunk[,input]) runs the chunk whole with its input
on stdin. An error inside a chunk reports on stderr and the call expands to nothing
rather than failing the run. s7 has no cli name and no argv companion.

s7 is the exception to the rename: it is one translation unit that ships no main of
its own, so guest/s7_main.c supplies the only visible symbol. It builds with the c
loader disabled, since the default under gcc reaches for dlopen, which an ape has not.
That entry point also hands the chunk a string port over its input instead of s7's own
stdin, whose read-line keeps the newline, answers an empty string at end of file, and
splits any line past 1023 bytes.

--- a/src/amk.h
+++ b/src/amk.h
@@ -20,5 +20,6 @@
 extern int gawk_main (int argc, char **argv);
 extern int jq_main (int argc, char **argv);
 extern int lua_run_main (int argc, char **argv);
+extern int s7_run_main (int argc, char **argv);

 #endif
--- a/src/function.c
+++ b/src/function.c
@@ -2502,6 +2502,9 @@
 #ifdef AMK_ENGINE_LUA
     { "lua", 0, lua_run_main, 0, 0, 0 },
 #endif
+#ifdef AMK_ENGINE_S7
+    { "s7", 0, s7_run_main, 0, 0, 0 },
+#endif
     { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 }
   };

